# Whitelist, not blacklist.
#
# What this repo ships is a Chrome extension with no build step: hand-written
# JS, CSS, HTML, a manifest and some icons. Nothing is generated, so anything
# that is not one of those is something that wandered in — an editor's scratch
# file, a zip of the packed extension, a stray note. Listing what is allowed
# keeps those out without having to guess at their names in advance.
#
# Everything is ignored, then the shipped file types are let back in. Git only
# looks inside a directory it has not ignored, so `!*/` is what lets it walk
# down to them at all; the last few lines shut the doors that opens.

*
!*/

# What the extension is made of.
!*.js
!*.css
!*.html
!*.json
!*.png
!*.svg
!*.woff2
!LICENSE
!.gitignore

# Prose. Every other .md stays ignored on purpose: notes, plans, summaries and
# generated write-ups do not belong in the tree, and a whitelist is the only
# way to keep them out without naming each one.
!README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Doors the whitelist above would otherwise leave open.

# Dependencies and packed builds are .js and .json too.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.zip
*.crx
*.xpi
*.pem

# Editor and tool state.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Local secrets, which are not covered by the extension list but cost nothing
# to name twice.
.env
.env*.local
